---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Restaurant",
  name: "Adorn Bar & Restaurant",
  servesCuisine: ["American", "Contemporary American"],
  priceRange: "$$$",
  url: "https://www.fourseasons.com/chicago/dining/restaurants/adorn/",
  address: {
    "@type": "PostalAddress",
    streetAddress: "120 E Delaware Pl, 7th Floor",
    addressLocality: "Chicago",
    addressRegion: "IL",
    postalCode: "60611",
    addressCountry: "US",
  },
  description:
    "Adorn Bar & Restaurant at Four Seasons Hotel Chicago — refined hotel dining on the 7th floor, led by executive chef Brent Balika.",
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Adorn Menu Guide (2026) — Hours, Chef, What to Order | Hotel Menu Guide"
  description="An independent guide to Adorn Bar & Restaurant at Four Seasons Hotel Chicago: hours, chef, open-evidence, and visiting tips. Adorn opened in October 2020 in the former Allium space; the restaurant publishes no menu prices online."
  path="/adorn-menu/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  ogImage="/images/adorn-dining.webp"
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    <img
      src="/images/adorn-dining.webp"
      alt="Illustration of a refined modern hotel dining room with jewel tones (illustrative, not the actual restaurant)"
      class="w-full h-64 sm:h-96 object-cover rounded-2xl mt-8"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />

    <p class="mt-8 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gold-dark">
      Menu Guide · Chicago
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mt-2 leading-tight">
      Adorn — Menu Guide
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      Adorn Bar &amp; Restaurant is the dining room of the Four Seasons Hotel Chicago, on
      the 7th floor at 120 E Delaware Pl. It opened on October 1, 2020 in the space of the
      former Allium, which had closed permanently — Adorn is its direct, on-site successor
      in the same room. The launch was a collaboration with James Beard award-winning chef
      Jonathon Sawyer (per a Four Seasons press release, September 2020); the current
      executive chef is Brent Balika (per the OpenTable listing, crawled ~mid-September
      2026). The restaurant holds a 4.8 OpenTable rating and serves all day, every day.
      Adorn publishes no menu prices online, so this guide covers what we verified:
      hours, chef, setting, and how to plan a visit. Everything is written in our own
      words.
    </p>

    <!-- At a glance -->
    <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="!mt-0 font-display text-xl font-bold">At a glance</h2>
      <dl class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 text-sm">
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Location</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">120 E Delaware Pl, 7th Floor, Chicago, IL 60611 (inside Four Seasons Hotel Chicago)</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Chef</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Executive chef Brent Balika (per OpenTable, ~Sep 2026; launch chef Jonathon Sawyer, 2020)</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Cuisine</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Refined contemporary hotel dining</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Hours</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Daily 7:00 AM–10:00 PM (OpenTable, ~Sep 2026)</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Reservations</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Bookable via OpenTable (4.8 rating, bookable September 2026 slots)</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">History</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Opened October 1, 2020 in the former Allium space (Allium closed permanently)</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-guide">
      <h2>Hours</h2>
      <p>
        Per the OpenTable listing crawled around mid-September 2026: <strong>open daily,
        7:00 AM–10:00 PM</strong> — breakfast through late-evening dinner, seven days a
        week. Live bookable inventory in September 2026 ("Booked 17 times today") confirms
        the restaurant is actively operating.
      </p>

      <h2>The concept</h2>
      <p>
        Adorn debuted October 1, 2020 as the Four Seasons Hotel Chicago's all-day
        restaurant, launched in collaboration with James Beard award-winning chef Jonathon
        Sawyer (Four Seasons press release, 2020-09-22). It occupies the same 7th-floor
        room that housed Allium until that restaurant closed permanently — one line of
        history, stated plainly: Allium is gone; Adorn is its successor.
      </p>

      <h2>Menu pricing</h2>
      <p>
        Adorn publishes no menu prices on its official page. We did not find a verifiable
        current price list in our research (October 2026), so we list none here rather
        than guess. Check the official Four Seasons page or the OpenTable listing before
        booking.
      </p>

      <h2>What to expect</h2>
      <p>From the verified open evidence, here's what we can tell you:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>All-day, every-day hours</strong> (7:00 AM–10:00 PM) — rare for a Magnificent Mile fine-dining room.</li>
        <li><strong>A 4.8 OpenTable rating</strong> with bookable slots in September 2026 — consistently well-reviewed by diners.</li>
        <li><strong>Chef Brent Balika</strong> leads the kitchen (per OpenTable, ~September 2026), following launch chef Jonathon Sawyer.</li>
        <li><strong>The same storied room</strong> that held Allium since its 2012 opening — Four Seasons' 7th-floor dining space on Delaware Place.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Planning your visit</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Book via OpenTable</strong> — the listing shows live inventory and a 4.8 rating across many reviews.</li>
        <li><strong>Morning or evening</strong>: with 7:00 AM opening, Adorn works for a hotel breakfast as easily as a full dinner.</li>
        <li><strong>Verify the menu</strong> on the official Four Seasons page before visiting, since prices and offerings aren't published.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Official links</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://www.fourseasons.com/chicago/dining/restaurants/adorn/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official restaurant page — Four Seasons Chicago</a> (menu info; no prices published online)</li>
        <li><a href="https://www.opentable.com/r/adorn-bar-and-restaurant-chicago" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Reservations — OpenTable</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Price disclaimer -->
    <div class="mt-10 rounded-xl border border-gold/40 bg-gold/10 p-5 text-sm text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      <p class="font-semibold text-ink mb-1">About these prices</p>
      <p>
        Adorn <strong>publishes no menu prices online</strong>, and our research (October
        2026) found no verifiable current price list — so this guide lists none rather
        than guessing. Menus and prices change frequently; always verify with the
        restaurant before visiting.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Related guides -->
    <div class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="!mt-0 font-display text-xl font-bold">More Chicago guides</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm">
        <li><a href="/best-hotel-restaurants-illinois/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">The best hotel restaurants in Illinois →</a></li>
        <li><a href="/torali-menu/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">Torali at the Ritz-Carlton</a> <span class="text-ink-soft">— modern Italian</span></li>
        <li><a href="/shanghai-terrace-menu/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">Shanghai Terrace at The Peninsula</a> <span class="text-ink-soft">— Cantonese</span></li>
        <li><a href="/travelle-menu/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">Travelle at The Langham</a> <span class="text-ink-soft">— river-view bistro</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-ink-soft">
      <a href="/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">← Back to all guides</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
